{%- comment -%}
  HA — Landing
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The holding page for the rebuild.

  Built 10 September 2026 from Aloha's mockup and her written type/colour spec.
  Rebuilt the same day against her second mockup, which changed four things:

    1. The headline copy — "...just like everything else here."
       (11 September, Angela: "The website" became "Our website", and
       "before it opens" became "before Hartwick opens".)
    2. The Porter statement line is gone. The setting stays (empty) so it can
       come back without code.
    3. The Junicode paragraph now sits beside the last line of the headline,
       right-aligned, instead of below it.
    4. The House Symbol and the contact line moved out of a full-width band at
       the foot of the page and into the text column, centred under the rule.
       The film now runs the full height of the page.

  Type, unchanged from her first spec:

    JUNICODE Bold    the headline           (700, uppercase, justified)
    PORTER Light     the statement          (300, uppercase — off by default)
    JUNICODE Light   the editorial paragraph (300, justified, last line right)
    NOTO SANS MONO CONDENSED Medium   the contact line (500)

    ink    #332820   (Peat Fibre — already in the palette)
    ground #F3F0E7   (Aloha's value; two points warmer and lighter than the
                      --ha-page-ground the rest of the site runs on, #F2EFE9.
                      Kept as her exact number and left as a section setting so
                      the two can be reconciled in one place later.)

  HOW THE PARAGRAPH SITS BESIDE THE HEADLINE. It is an ordinary block in normal
  flow, pulled up by a fraction of one headline line so it lands in the empty
  space to the right of the short last line. It is NOT floated: a float would
  have to come before the headline in the markup, which would hand a screen
  reader the paragraph before the h1 on a page that has only three elements on
  it. The lift is applied only from 1100px up, where the headline reliably
  breaks with a short last line; below that the paragraph simply sits under the
  headline, which is what it does on a phone anyway. `copy_lift` turns it off.

  PORTER AND PUNCTUATION. Porter is subset to uppercase A-Z and space only —
  the brand rule is that it carries no numbers, punctuation or symbols. Any
  punctuation in the statement line renders in Junicode. That is the type
  system behaving as designed, not a fallback failure.

  THE FILM. `Scrapbook LANDING03.mp4`, re-encoded to 810x1440, 8.2s, 2.4 MB —
  is served from theme assets. The delivered file was 1080x1920 and 8.0 MB
  with an AAC track it never used; at 6 fps of collage stills the codec had
  nothing to reuse between frames, so the weight was all in the pixels. It
  was re-encoded 11 September 2026 after Aloha reported it not playing on
  mobile: audio stripped, three-quarter scale, CRF 27, index at the front.
  Visually identical at 1:1. A video with no audio track is also the most
  reliable autoplay case on iOS — nothing for a power-saving policy to refuse.
  Portrait is the right shape for this column, which is why it survives the
  crop here where the 16:9 homepage hero did not. It is muted, looping and
  inert: no controls, no sound, nothing to click. Under
  prefers-reduced-motion the video is not rendered at all and the poster image
  stands in its place, so the page still reads for anyone who has asked their
  system for stillness.

  Everything is a setting. No copy, colour or asset is hard-coded, so Aloha can
  change any of it in the theme editor without coming back to me.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign ink = section.settings.ink
  assign ground = section.settings.ground
  assign rule = ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.22
  assign lift = section.settings.copy_lift | divided_by: 100.0
  assign has_video = false
  if section.settings.video_shopify != blank or section.settings.video_asset != blank
    assign has_video = true
  endif
-%}

{% style %}
  {%- comment -%}
    The ground is painted on the page itself, not only on the section.

    The section covers the viewport, so for a while this looked like it did not
    matter. It does: the landing layout paints the body from the site-wide
    `ha_page_ground`, which is #F2EFE9 — a different, cooler cream from Aloha's
    #F3F0E7. The wrong one shows wherever the section does not reach: the
    rubber-band overscroll at the top and bottom of the page on macOS and iOS,
    the strip left when a mobile browser's address bar collapses and the visual
    viewport grows past 100svh, and the browser chrome tint from theme-color.

    Declaring it here keeps ONE source of truth — the section's own Background
    setting — instead of two values that agree only by coincidence.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  html,
  body.ha-landing-body { background: {{ ground }}; }

  .ha-landing {
    /* 2 October 2026: the site moved to Troja / Porter / Typewriter, but the
       landing page is its own earlier design and stays exempt, so it keeps
       the faces it was drawn with. */
    --ha-font-narrate:  "Junicode", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    --ha-font-record:   var(--ha-font-mono);
    --ha-font-identify: {% if settings.ha_porter_licensed %}"Porter", {% endif %}"Junicode", Georgia, serif;
    --ha-landing-ink: {{ ink }};
    --ha-landing-ground: {{ ground }};
    --ha-landing-rule: {{ rule }};

    /* The headline metrics are variables because the paragraph's lift is
       measured in headline lines — the two have to stay tied together. */
    --ha-landing-display: clamp(1.75rem, 3.3vw, 3.35rem);
    --ha-landing-display-lh: 1.16;

    /* One rhythm unit. The mockup spaces rule, symbol and contact line at an
       even ~54px at 1450px wide; this is that measure, made fluid. */
    --ha-landing-gap: clamp(1.75rem, 3.7vw, 3.4rem);

    box-sizing: border-box;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-height: 100vh;
    min-height: 100svh;
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--ha-landing-ground);
    color: var(--ha-landing-ink);
  }
  .ha-landing *,
  .ha-landing *::before,
  .ha-landing *::after { box-sizing: inherit; }

  .ha-landing__body {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  /* --- the film ---------------------------------------------------------- */
  .ha-landing__media {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--ha-landing-ground);
    /* Mobile: the 9:16 clip at full bleed would push the headline off the
       first screen, so it is capped and cropped rather than left to run. */
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
  }
  .ha-landing__media-fill {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center {{ section.settings.media_focus }}%;
    display: block;
  }
  .ha-landing__media video.ha-landing__media-fill { z-index: 1; }
  .ha-landing__media--empty {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--ha-landing-rule);
  }
  .ha-landing__media-note {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-record);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.55;
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* --- the text column --------------------------------------------------- */
  .ha-landing__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: {{ section.settings.text_position }};
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(1.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
  }
  .ha-landing__column {
    width: 100%;
    /* THE MEASURE. Justified setting stretches the word spaces to fill the
       line, so the wider the column the wider the gaps — Aloha's "a lot of
       space in the Header". The fix is the measure, not the type size: bring
       the column in until the headline's natural width nearly fills it and
       justification has almost nothing left to stretch.

       It is set in headline ems, NOT in rem, and that matters. The headline is
       fluid (3.3vw between its two clamp stops), so a measure fixed in rem
       would hold still while the type shrank under it — and the gaps would open
       straight back up on any screen narrower than the one it was tuned on. Tied
       to the display size, the ratio of natural line width to column width is
       the same at every viewport, so the spacing that was tuned at 1450px is the
       spacing you get at 1200px and at 2560px. */
    max-width: calc(var(--ha-landing-display) * {{ section.settings.measure }});
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .ha-landing__heading {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-narrate);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: var(--ha-landing-display);
    line-height: var(--ha-landing-display-lh);
    letter-spacing: 0.005em;
    margin: 0;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .ha-landing__body-copy {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-narrate);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(0.875rem, 1.05vw, {{ section.settings.copy_size }}px);
    line-height: 1.7;
    letter-spacing: 0.005em;
    margin: var(--ha-landing-gap) 0 0;
  }

  .ha-landing__statement {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-identify);
    font-weight: 300;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: clamp(0.8rem, 1.05vw, 1rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    letter-spacing: 0.035em;
    margin: var(--ha-landing-gap) 0 0;
  }

  .ha-landing__rule {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ha-landing-rule);
    margin: var(--ha-landing-gap) 0 0;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .ha-landing__symbol {
    display: block;
    width: {{ section.settings.symbol_size }}px;
    height: auto;
    margin: var(--ha-landing-gap) auto 0;
  }

  .ha-landing__contact {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-record);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(0.75rem, 0.85vw, 0.85rem);
    line-height: 1.75;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    /* RECORD is an uppercase voice everywhere else on the site. Here it is not:
       the mockup sets this line in sentence case, and an email address that has
       been uppercased is a different address to read. */
    text-transform: none;
    text-align: center;
    margin: var(--ha-landing-gap) auto 0;
    max-width: 34rem;
  }
  .ha-landing__contact a {
    /* The mockup sets the address on its own line under the sentence, so the
       break is declared rather than left to the width of the viewport. */
    display: block;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    width: fit-content;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .ha-landing__contact a:hover,
  .ha-landing__contact a:focus-visible { border-bottom-color: currentColor; }

  /* The cookie preferences link, in the contact line's voice but quieter and
     tighter to it: a legal necessity on the page, not part of the composition.
     The holding page has no footer, so this is where it lives. */
  .ha-landing__cookie {
    margin-top: calc(var(--ha-landing-gap) / 2);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* --- desktop ----------------------------------------------------------- */
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ha-landing__body {
      grid-template-columns: {{ section.settings.media_width }}% 1fr;
    }
    .ha-landing__media { aspect-ratio: auto; }
    .ha-landing__text {
      padding-left: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
      padding-right: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    }
    /* Justified setting is what gives the mockup its even word-spread. It is
       held back on narrow screens, where justifying a line of four uppercase
       words opens rivers instead of closing them. */
    .ha-landing__heading {
      text-align: justify;
      text-justify: inter-word;
      text-wrap: initial;
    }
    .ha-landing__body-copy {
      width: {{ section.settings.copy_width }}%;
      margin-left: auto;
      text-align: justify;
      text-justify: inter-word;
      text-align-last: right;
    }
  }

  {%- if section.settings.copy_lift > 0 -%}
    /* The lift that puts the paragraph beside the last line of the headline.

       At 60% the paragraph's first baseline lands on the headline's last
       baseline — Aloha's "align it next to the full stop". That number is
       measured, not eyeballed: it is the heading's half-leading plus descent,
       plus the paragraph's ascent, over one heading line. Both terms are shares
       of their own type size, so the alignment drifts by about 2px across the
       whole desktop range rather than coming apart.

       Held back below 1100px, where the headline's last line is no longer
       reliably short enough to leave room for the paragraph at all. */
    @media screen and (min-width: 1100px) {
      .ha-landing__body-copy {
        margin-top: calc(var(--ha-landing-display) * var(--ha-landing-display-lh) * -{{ lift }});
      }
    }
  {%- endif -%}

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .ha-landing__media video { display: none; }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<div class="ha-landing">
  <div class="ha-landing__body">
    <div class="ha-landing__media{% unless has_video or section.settings.poster != blank %} ha-landing__media--empty{% endunless %}">
      {%- if section.settings.poster != blank -%}
        {{
          section.settings.poster
          | image_url: width: 1200
          | image_tag:
            loading: 'eager',
            fetchpriority: 'high',
            widths: '400, 600, 800, 1000, 1200',
            sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw',
            class: 'ha-landing__media-fill',
            alt: section.settings.media_alt
        }}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.video_shopify != blank -%}
        {{
          section.settings.video_shopify
          | video_tag:
            image_size: '1200x',
            autoplay: true,
            loop: true,
            muted: true,
            controls: false,
            class: 'ha-landing__media-fill'
        }}
      {%- elsif section.settings.video_asset != blank -%}
        <video
          class="ha-landing__media-fill"
          autoplay
          muted
          loop
          playsinline
          disablepictureinpicture
          preload="auto"
          tabindex="-1"
          aria-hidden="true"
          {% if section.settings.poster != blank %}poster="{{ section.settings.poster | image_url: width: 1200 }}"{% endif %}
        >
          <source src="{{ section.settings.video_asset | asset_url }}" type="video/mp4">
        </video>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- unless has_video or section.settings.poster != blank -%}
        <p class="ha-landing__media-note">{{ section.settings.media_placeholder }}</p>
      {%- endunless -%}
    </div>

    <div class="ha-landing__text">
      <div class="ha-landing__column">
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h1 class="ha-landing__heading">
            {{- section.settings.heading | escape | newline_to_br -}}
          </h1>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.body_copy != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-landing__body-copy">
            {{- section.settings.body_copy | escape | newline_to_br -}}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.statement != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-landing__statement">
            {{- section.settings.statement | escape | newline_to_br -}}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.show_rule -%}
          <hr class="ha-landing__rule">
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.symbol != blank -%}
          {{
            section.settings.symbol
            | image_url: width: 300
            | image_tag: class: 'ha-landing__symbol', alt: shop.name, loading: 'lazy'
          }}
        {%- elsif section.settings.show_symbol -%}
          <img
            class="ha-landing__symbol"
            src="{{ 'ha-house-symbol-black.png' | asset_url }}"
            alt="{{ shop.name | escape }}"
            width="1867"
            height="1867"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- endif -%}

        <p class="ha-landing__contact">
          {{- section.settings.contact_label | escape -}}
          {%- if section.settings.contact_email != blank %}
            <a href="mailto:{{ section.settings.contact_email | strip }}">{{ section.settings.contact_email | strip }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>

        {%- if section.settings.show_cookie_preferences -%}
          <p class="ha-landing__contact ha-landing__cookie">
            {%- render 'ha-cookie-preferences', label: section.settings.cookie_preferences_label -%}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HA — Landing",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "ha-landing-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Film"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "video_asset",
      "label": "Video file in theme assets",
      "default": "ha-landing-scrapbook.mp4",
      "info": "Filename only. Currently Scrapbook LANDING03.mp4, re-encoded for mobile (810×1440, 8.2s, 2.4 MB, no audio). Clear this to fall back to the still image alone."
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video_shopify",
      "label": "Video from Shopify Files (optional)",
      "info": "If set, this is used instead of the theme asset above. Preferred once the clip is uploaded to Content › Files — Shopify then serves it in several sizes."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "poster",
      "label": "Still image",
      "info": "Shown before the video loads, and instead of it for visitors who have asked their system to reduce motion. A frame from the clip is ideal."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "media_alt",
      "label": "Still image alt text",
      "info": "Describe the image for screen readers. Required before this page goes public."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "media_placeholder",
      "label": "Placeholder label",
      "default": "Landing film",
      "info": "Shown only while there is no video and no image."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "media_width",
      "label": "Film width (desktop)",
      "min": 30,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 42
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "media_focus",
      "label": "Vertical crop",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 50,
      "info": "0% keeps the top of the frame, 100% keeps the bottom."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Text"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Headline",
      "default": "Our website is being rebuilt, by hand, just like everything else here.",
      "info": "Junicode Bold. Set in uppercase by the stylesheet — type it in sentence case."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "body_copy",
      "label": "Paragraph",
      "default": "A new home for the Material Record: the fibres, the Masters, the pieces themselves. Write to us directly before Hartwick opens.",
      "info": "Junicode Light. Sits beside the last line of the headline on a wide screen, under it on a narrow one."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "measure",
      "label": "Text column width",
      "min": 8,
      "max": 18,
      "step": 0.5,
      "unit": "em",
      "default": 12,
      "info": "Measured in headline ems, so the word spacing holds at every screen width. Narrower means tighter spacing, because justified type has less to stretch. 12 is measured, not guessed — it is the narrowest that still holds the headline on four lines. Below about 11.5 it breaks to five and the spacing opens up badly. Type a line break into the headline to force a break of your own."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "copy_size",
      "label": "Paragraph size",
      "min": 13,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 15
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "copy_width",
      "label": "Paragraph width (desktop)",
      "min": 40,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 70
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "copy_lift",
      "label": "Paragraph lift",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 60,
      "info": "How far the paragraph rises into the space beside the headline's last line, as a share of one headline line. 60% is measured: it is the value that puts the paragraph's first baseline exactly on the headline's last baseline, so the sentence sits level with the full stop rather than below it. 0% drops it back under the headline. Applies from 1100px wide up."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "statement",
      "label": "Statement (Porter)",
      "info": "Porter Light, uppercase. Empty in the current design — the second mockup drops it. Punctuation renders in Junicode; Porter carries none by brand rule."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_rule",
      "label": "Show the hairline",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "text_position",
      "label": "Vertical position",
      "options": [
        { "value": "flex-start", "label": "Top" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "Centre" },
        { "value": "flex-end", "label": "Bottom" }
      ],
      "default": "flex-end",
      "info": "The mockup sits the whole column low in the page. Centre it here if it reads better on a tall screen."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Mark and contact"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_symbol",
      "label": "Show the House Symbol",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "symbol",
      "label": "House Symbol override",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's own black House Symbol."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "symbol_size",
      "label": "House Symbol width",
      "min": 28,
      "max": 120,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 66
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "contact_label",
      "label": "Contact line",
      "default": "For appointments, wholesale and press enquiries:"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "contact_email",
      "label": "Email address",
      "default": "contact@hartwickatelier.com"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_cookie_preferences",
      "label": "Show the cookie preferences link",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Under the contact line. Reopens the cookie banner from Settings > Customer privacy so a visitor can change their choice. The holding page has no footer, so this is the permanent link Angela asked for (14 September 2026)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cookie_preferences_label",
      "label": "Cookie preferences label",
      "default": "Cookie preferences"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "ink",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "#332820"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "ground",
      "label": "Background",
      "default": "#F3F0E7"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "HA — Landing"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
